==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|deterreo|dēterreō|deter, discourage|lang=la}} < {{term|lang=la|de||from}} + {{term|lang=la|terreo|terreō|I frighten}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-deter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|deter|r|ing}}

# To [[prevent]] something from happening.
# To [[persuade]] someone not to do something; to [[discourage]].
#* '''1748'''.  David Hume.  ''Enquiries concerning the human understanding and concerning the principles of moral.'' London: Oxford University Press, 1973.  § 10.
#*: we have in following enquiry, attempted to throw some light upon subjects, from which uncertainty has hitherto '''deterred''' the wise

